        "body": "R5: a user volume change that lands between a duck-ramp step's get-volume and its next set-volume is overwritten, the ramp runs on to 20 % and the restore puts the pre-take volume back (4-5 of 16 swept offsets, two passes; other offsets give up correctly). Private null sink behind a wpctl guard shim, which widens the window. Evidence: .flow/tmp/qa-fn-85-delivery-that-leaves-the-desktop-as-it/runs/r5-race-p1/, runs/r5-race-p2/, runs/r5-media-p3/wpctl.log (M4). Memory: .flow/memory/bug/runtime-errors/duck-ramp-overwrites-a-volume-the-user-2026-11-01.md (surface: crates/dettivod/src/media.rs (ramp))",
